            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pamela van Bloois"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very simple and fresh tasting. I did add about a tablespoon of melted butter only because powdered sugar can have a chalky-like under tone with too few ingredients. This was perfect as a glaze over a deep chocolate cake."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carlos Lucero"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm glad I read the review by Pamela. I also added a tablespoon of melted salted butter, as well as two tablespoons plus one teaspoon of freshly squeezed orange juice. And I went ahead and used the entire orange for zest. That came out to be around one tablespoon of zest. I really think that the salted butter cut down a little bit on the sweetness which I thought was way too sweet.",
            "datePublished": "2021-01-22T03:13:13.913Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Munderwho"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The recipe is on to something but it needs work: The addition of butter is critical since without it the glaze lacks body. Plus, as stated above, much more juice is needed to achieve a glaze consistency.",
            "datePublished": "2013-11-24T07:26:00.293Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gina Kiyuna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’m reading the reviews, I added the juice and zest of the whole orange, as well as about 2 tablespoons of melted salted butter. Whisked until smooth. Poured this over our store bought original flavor crepe cake (from Costco). Made it kinda like a Crepe Suzette cake!",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-06T03:15:07.473Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Emily"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great simple recipe. I put it on a chocolate-orange marble cake. I love the orange, so I added a little more than 2 teaspoons of zest, and I wanted a less thick consistency so upped the orange juice to 2 tablespoons. Also followed previous suggestions of adding 1 tablespoon of melted butter. Definitely will use again, and maybe try it with lemon instead.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-03T00:21:20.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gabby K"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added about 4 tablespoons of fresh orange juice and 1/4 teaspoon more of orange zest. I used this to cover a Martha Stewart's orange yogurt cake and it was amazing!",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-24T03:47:42.887Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LVW"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had to add 2 extra tablespoons of oj to make it into a glaze. I also added more zest for it to have flavor. It did have a chalky taste. I'm sorry I didn't read the reviews before I made it and add butter. What I did was add a couple drops of orange extract to overcome that taste and it was good after that.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-01T15:19:28.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "John Zylma"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this to put on cranberry pecan scones I made. Worked great. I added a little bit more Orange Juice to flavor it more and thin it to me he right consistency. I wanted it thin enough to put on hot scones so it would run over and down the sides. It was perfect. And tasted just right.",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-23T04:26:50.170Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Laura S"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love how uber easy this recipe was to make and a great compliment to my cranberry-orange muffins!!! I will say 1tbsp of OJ is not enough, but it's such a good starting point to gage your preferred consistency. I used approx 2 1/2 tbsps of OJ, and was PERFECT! As it glided down the muffin top, it began to stiffen and left a beautifully glazed muffin. Though after seeing the results, I was disappointed I did not have scones on hand to glaze. I'll DEFINITELY be using this recipe again.",
            "datePublished": "2014-05-10T15:23:43.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LVPERRY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Outstanding and perfect topper for pumpkin bread and cookies. I too added the tbsp of butter and it hardens to a nice shiny glaze that tastes fresh. Great simple recipe. Thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-18T22:32:13.137Z"
          },
          {
